  "name": "TISSUE TRANSGLUTAMINASE  TTG - DGP SCREEN",
  "code": "2852",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><strong>Negative Results (below cutoff):</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\">Strongly suggest absence of active celiac disease if the patient has not already started a gluten-free diet.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\">Negative serology with high suspicion: consider additional genetic or histopathologic testing.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><strong>Equivocal/Borderline:</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\">May indicate early-stage disease, partial adherence to a gluten-free diet, or analytical variability.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\">Repeat after a few weeks and correlate with symptoms and dietary history.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><strong>Positive Results (above cutoff):</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\">Strongly suggest active celiac disease, especially if both tTG and DGP are elevated.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\">Confirmatory endoscopic biopsy recommended for diagnosis.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\">In IgA deficiency, reliance on IgG-based results is necessary.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><strong>DGP Antibodies:</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\">Helpful as adjunct, especially in cases with negative tTG and high clinical suspicion, in young children (&lt;3 years), or known IgA deficiency.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
  "showInterpretation": false,
  "sampleType": "serum",
